uying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Moog Inc. designs, manufactures, and integrates precision motion and fluid controls and controls systems for original equipment manufacturers and end users in the aerospace, defense, and industrial markets in the United States, Germany, and internationally. The company operates through four segments: Space and Defense, Military Aircraft, Commercial Aircraft, and Industrial. Its Space and Defense segment provides critical defense components and motion-control systems used in defense vehicle platforms, missile systems, naval ships and submarines; high-performance components and systems used for space launch vehicles, satellites and spacecraft vehicles. The Military Aircraft segment designs, manufacture and integrate primary and secondary flight controls, mission-critical actuation systems, and products for various military fixed-wing aircraft and rotorcraft for both original equipment manufacturers and aftermarket customers. The Commercial Aircraft segment designs, manufactures, and integrates flight-critical control systems and products for various commercial aircraft including widebody, narrowbody, business jets and regional jets. The company's Industrial segment provides customized and high-performance motion control components and systems for industrial automation, medical, simulation, and test and energy applications, including precision components used in heavy machinery, medical devices and components, power generation products, as well as simulation platforms for flight training and material testing applications. The company was formerly known as Moog Valve Company. Moog Inc. was incorporated in 1951 and is headquartered in East Aurora, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Patrick J. Roche | President, CEO & Director | Age 62 | Compensation: $2.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 14K people. Revenue per employee of $323K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $22K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Moog Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $10.6B market cap on $4.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 29%.","The business throws off $307M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.06\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 9.5\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.6%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 64% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6425734650422792},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Moog (MOG.A) Could Be 25% Undervalued Following Record Results And 2027 Guidance","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-mog.a/moog/news/moog-moga-could-be-25-undervalued-following-record-results-a","date":"2026-11-22","timestamp":1795378068.015,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.796,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Will Record Earnings Guidance Change Moog Stock Narrative","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-mog.a/moog/news/will-record-earnings-guidance-change-moog-stock-narrative","date":"2026-11-21","timestamp":1795288058.988,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.66,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Moog Inc (MOG.A) (Q4 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Record Fiscal 2026 Results and a Cautious ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/moog-inc-mog-q4-2026-230050624.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795215650.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.586,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Don't Ignore The Insider Selling In Moog","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capita